    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a subject I find both challenging and fascinating. While it doesn't come naturally to me like biology does, I enjoy the logical structure and problem-solving aspects of math. It's a subject where I feel I can grow and improve with practice, even if it takes more effort than other topics.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "I do experience some anxiety when faced with complex mathematical problems, especially those that require abstract thinking or involve advanced concepts like calculus. However, this anxiety is usually temporary and diminishes as I break down the problem into smaller, more manageable parts. I find that taking breaks and approaching the subject methodically helps me overcome this.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used an AI-powered math tutor app last year to help me with algebra. The experience was mixed; while the app provided clear explanations and step-by-step solutions, it sometimes felt impersonal compared to working with a human tutor. However, it was convenient and helped me learn at my own pace.",
